    <div class="hcm-or-wrap-sm">
      <div class="hcm-or-hd"><span class="hcm-or-eyebrow">Expert Analysis</span><h2>Expert Editorial Summary: Kyota Massage Chair Reviews</h2></div>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px">After working with buyers exploring Kyota massage chairs — from first-time shoppers to value-focused upgraders — the HCM product team has observed clear, consistent patterns in how customers experience the brand.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">General Customer Satisfaction:</strong> Kyota massage chairs earn positive satisfaction across most buyer categories. The brand's defining strength is its approachable comfort, clear model progression from the Genki M380 to the Nokori M980 Syner-D, and strong value positioning at each tier.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Strongest Features:</strong> Three qualities consistently rise to the top: <span class="hcm-or-mark">everyday comfort and ease of use</span>, <span class="hcm-or-mark">value for money</span>, and <span class="hcm-or-mark">practical auto programs</span>.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Most Common Expectation Gaps:</strong> The most frequent gap involves foot roller intensity — sensitive users should start at lower settings. Some buyers expecting ultra-premium customization across all models should review feature differences between tiers carefully.</p>
      <p style="margin-bottom:18px"><strong style="color:var(--ink)">Pre-Purchase Recommendations:</strong></p>
      <ol style="padding-left:1.5rem;margin-bottom:18px;font-size:15px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.8;list-style:decimal">
        <li>Try the chair in person at an HCM showroom if possible</li>
        <li>Measure your space carefully — even compact models need recline clearance</li>
        <li>Start at lower intensity and foot roller settings during the first few sessions</li>
        <li>Discuss your comfort goals, budget, and space with an HCM specialist</li>
        <li>Understand that heat therapy is a comfort enhancement, not medical treatment</li>
      </ol>
